# Horizontal cutting plane at z=0, normal = (0,0,-1)  (winding reversed vs knife_horiz)
#
# Regression test: the triangle normal is exactly -UnitZ (anti-parallel to Z).
# The cross product n.cross(UnitZ) is again the zero vector, but this time the
# rotation angle is pi rather than 0, so AngleAxisd(pi, NaN_axis) produces a
# NaN rotation matrix.  Bug 2's fix detects the near-zero axis and substitutes
# UnitX as the rotation axis, giving a valid 180-degree flip.
#
# Geometrically identical to knife_horiz but with face normals pointing downward.

v -3  3 0
v  3  3 0
v  3 -3 0
v -3 -3 0

f 1 2 3
f 1 3 4
